", "t": [["patch", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\wordfreq-1794053258\\wordfreq.py","old_string":"","new_string":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Count word frequencies in a UTF-8 text file.\n\nUsage: python wordfreq.py FILE [-n N] [--min-len K]\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n\ndef positive_int(value):\n    \"\"\"argparse type: must parse as an integer strictly greater than zero.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        number = int(value)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError(f\"invalid integer: {value!r}\")\n    if number <= 0:\n        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError(f\"must be a positive integer, got {value!r}\")\n    return number\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    \"\"\"Yield lower-cased words: maximal runs of letters (any Unicode letter)\n    and ASCII apostrophes, with outer apostrophes stripped. Empty results are\n    skipped; digits and underscores are not part of words.\"\"\"\n    word = []\n    for ch in text:\n        if ch.isalpha() or ch == \"'\":\n            word.append(ch)\n        else:\n            if word:\n                token = \"\".join(word).lower().strip(\"'\")\n                if token:\n                    yield token\n                word = []\n    if word:\n        token = \"\".join(word).lower().strip(\"'\")\n        if token:\n            yield token\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        prog=\"wordfreq.py\",\n        description=\"Print the N most frequent words in FILE (word count, most frequent first; ties alphabetical).\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"file\", help=\"input file, read as UTF-8\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-n\", type=positive_int, default=10, metavar=\"N\",\n                        help=\"number of words to print (default: 10)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--min-len\", type=positive_int, default=1, metavar=\"K\",\n                        help=\"ignore words shorter than K characters (default: 1)\")\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    try:\n        with open(args.file, encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n            text = handle.read()\n    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):\n        print(f\"error: cannot read {args.file}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    counts = Counter()\n    for token in tokenize(text):\n        if len(token) >= args.min_len:\n            counts[token] += 1\n\n    ranked = sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0]))[: args.n]\n\n    reconfigure = getattr(sys.stdout, \"reconfigure\", None)\n    if reconfigure is not None:\n        sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for word, count in ranked:\n        print(f\"{word} {count}\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}"]]}

{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class where each instance maintains its own accounts dictionary. The open_account method validates that the account doesn't already exist and the initial balance is non-negative, raising ValueError if either check fails. For deposits, I need to validate that the amount is positive first, then check if the account exists—both the amount validation and account existence checks need to happen before any mutation occurs.

Withdraw validates the amount is positive, retrieves the balance from the account (raising KeyError if missing), and raises InsufficientFunds if the balance is less than the withdrawal amount. Transfer validates the amount, checks that source and destination aren't the same, verifies both accounts exist by accessing them, checks for sufficient funds, then performs the transfer. I'll add an InsufficientFunds exception class that inherits from ValueError, and create a module-level default_bank instance with wrapper functions for backwards compatibility. I should also ensure amounts are treated as integers by default and include a docstring in the module.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of accounts; two instances never share accounts.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial balance must be >= 0: \" + repr(initial))\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: \" + repr(amount))\n        self._require(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: \" + repr(amount))\n        current = self._require(name)\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has balance %s, cannot withdraw %s\" % (name, current, amount))\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._require(name)\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: \" + repr(amount))\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + src)\n        src_balance = self._require(src)\n        dst_balance = self._require(dst)\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has balance %s, cannot transfer %s\" % (src, src_balance, amount))\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] = dst_balance + amount\n\n    def _require(self, name):\n        try:\n            return self._accounts[name]\n        except KeyError:\n            raise KeyError(\"unknown account: \" + repr(name))\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

